          "text": "```java\n/**\n * Consonants from the same code group separated by W or H are treated as one.\n *\n * @throws EncoderException\n */\n@Test\npublic void testHWRuleEx3() throws EncoderException {\n    final Soundex soundex = createStringEncoder();\n\n    // B, F, P, and V share the same Soundex code.\n    Assert.assertEquals(\"B000\", soundex.encode(\"BHB\"));\n    Assert.assertEquals(\"B000\", soundex.encode(\"BWB\"));\n    Assert.assertEquals(\"B000\", soundex.encode(\"BHF\"));\n    Assert.assertEquals(\"B000\", soundex.encode(\"BWF\"));\n\n    // S and C share a code even when separated by H.\n    Assert.assertEquals(\"A261\", soundex.encode(\"Ashcraft\"));\n    Assert.assertEquals(\"A261\", soundex.encode(\"Ashcroft\"));\n\n    // Unlike H and W, a vowel separates otherwise identical codes.\n    Assert.assertEquals(\"B100\", soundex.encode(\"BAB\"));\n}\n```"
        }
